  "summary": "São Paulo State University (Unesp) is a public, state-run university established in 1976 by bringing together independent colleges across São Paulo state. Its oldest predecessor dates to 1923. Today, it serves more than 45,000 students across 23 campuses and 33 academic units in inland, coastal, and capital-city locations.\n\nUnesp offers 171 undergraduate course options and a broad range of postgraduate programs. Its facilities include 30 libraries, about 1,900 laboratories, hospitals and clinics, museums, and five experimental farms. Research priorities include bioenergy, biotechnology, climate change, nanotechnology, public policy, and marine sciences. The university also maintains international exchange and cooperation agreements with institutions in 52 countries.\n\nThe university is governed by a rector and a University Council, while individual institutes have some autonomy. Undergraduate admissions are through a competitive state-wide exam, with additional tests for some programs. Rankings cited in the article place Unesp among Brazil’s leading universities and recognize its research output and international standing. Its alumni and faculty include artists, scientists, academics, and public figures.",
